# Findings accepted on purpose. Read by Trivy in scan-images.yml.
# Give every entry a reason and an expiry date (exp:YYYY-MM-DD), so the scan
# reports it again if the cause hasn't been fixed by then.

# certbot/certbot: Python libraries in the upstream image, not fixed in any
# certbot release yet (v5.10.0 of 2026-11-10 is the newest). Hardly reachable:
# certbot only runs to renew certificates and only talks to Let's Encrypt.
# Delete these once a certbot release fixes them and Dependabot has bumped it.
#
# urllib3: TLS interception through an HTTPS proxy (none is configured).
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-12-31
# urllib3: DoS via unbounded memory.
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-12-31
# msgpack: DoS and an out-of-bounds read when unpacking crafted data.
CVE-2026-114613 exp:2026-12-31
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-12-31
# setuptools: path traversal when installing packages, which never happens here.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-12-31

# ghcr.io/versatiles-org/photon: libraries inside photon.jar of komoot/photon
# 1.3.0, the newest release. Upstream master updates them (OpenSearch 3.9,
# Javalin 7.2.3, jackson 3.2.3) but hasn't released that yet. Delete these
# after upgrading to the next release; mind the OpenSearch upgrade (README,
# "Upgrading Photon").
#
# Photon listens only on 127.0.0.1, behind nginx, which forwards plain
# HTTP/1.1. Its HTTP API runs on Jetty (Javalin); netty belongs to the
# embedded OpenSearch, whose ports aren't published.
#
# netty-handler: SNI routing bypass (CRITICAL). No TLS reaches Photon.
CVE-2026-75595 exp:2026-12-31
# netty-codec-http, -http2, -http3: DoS via SPDY, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3.
CVE-2026-55831 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-55833 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56745 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56819 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-56816 exp:2026-12-31
# netty-codec-compression: infinite loop while decompressing.
CVE-2026-59901 exp:2026-12-31
# jetty-security: authentication bypass. Photon uses no authentication.
CVE-2026-10050 exp:2026-12-31
# jackson-core and jackson-databind (2.x and 3.x): DoS on crafted JSON. Not
# ruled out, but Photon's API takes query parameters, not JSON.
CVE-2026-89407 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-89425 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-68497 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-91776 exp:2026-12-31
CVE-2026-91777 exp:2026-12-31
